I've written the plan as two task files and an issue-responses note in session_plan/. The commit step didn't record them, because session_plan/ is gitignored. The planned command ends in || true, so the harness expects that and reads the files from disk.

Task 01 (product, my own pick, kept outside cli as the trajectory asked): fail fast when a local server refuses the connection.
• The problem: today's assessment measured it. With nothing listening on Ollama's default port, yoyo --provider ollama -p hi retries for 70 seconds before it errors. --base-url http://127.0.0.1:9 takes 69 seconds.
• The change: when the host is loopback and the connection is refused, yoyo allows one retry, then stops. It prints a message naming the refused URL. Remote hosts and every other error keep exactly the old retry path.
• Size limits: the new logic goes in a new module, src/prompt/loopback_refused.rs, because src/prompt_retry.rs is already at its size cap. src/prompt.rs's entry in tests/module_size.rs gets updated to its new line count.
• Tests: the table includes the near-misses: a remote refusal (where retrying can work), a loopback timeout, and localhost.example.com. A real-binary test runs against a closed port and checks the exit code, the wall time and the URL in stderr.
• Left for later: two defects on the same path (/retry printed in -p mode, and a raw reqwest error dump) aren't fixed here. The task files them as an issue before the push unless an open ticket already holds them.

Task 02 (backlog drain, Fixes #1108): show sub-agent spend in `/cost`.
• The problem: /cost's per-turn breakdown still counts only the main agent's own spend, while /tokens and the JSON output already include sub-agents.
• The change: a separate block after the per-turn table shows each prompt's delegated spend and a total. It says plainly that the split is per prompt, not per turn, because sub-agent spend is only recorded once per prompt today.
• Unchanged output: a session that never used a sub-agent gets byte-identical /cost output.
• Size limits: nothing gets added to src/format/cost.rs, which is at its size cap.
• Fallback: if the block can't be built, the commit says "Part of #1108" rather than closing the ticket.

